"2260","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Nuʿmān al-Suhaymī, who said: Qays ibn Ṭalq came to me in Ramaḍān during the last part of the night, after I had withdrawn my hands from the pre-dawn meal (suḥūr) for fear of dawn. He requested some food from me, so I said: ""O my uncle! If there had remained for you any portion of the night, I would have taken you to food and drink I have."" He said: ""You have it?"" So he entered, and I brought near to him tharīd (bread soaked in broth), meat, and nabīdh. He ate and drank, and he compelled me, so I ate and drank, while I was apprehensive of dawn. Then he said: Ṭalq ibn ʿAlī narrated to me that the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Eat and drink, and let not the ascending white light deceive you; so eat and drink until the redness appears to you horizontally."""
