"2275","Kahmas al-Hilali narrated: ""I embraced Islam, so I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informed him of my Islam. I stayed for a year, during which I became emaciated and my body wasted away. [Then I came to him again.] He lowered his gaze, then raised it. I said: 'Do you not recognize me?' He said: 'And who are you?' I said: 'I am Kahmas al-Hilali.' He said: 'What has brought you to the state I see?' I said: 'I have not broken my fast during the day since [meeting] you, nor have I slept at night.' He said: 'And who commanded you to torture yourself?! Fast the month of patience (Ramadan), and one day of every month.' I said: 'Increase me.' He said: 'Fast the month of patience, and two days of every month.' I said: 'Increase me, for I find strength.' He said: 'Fast the month of patience, and three days of every month.'"""
